---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/settings';
const affiliateActive = settings.affiliateMode === 'affiliate' && Boolean(settings.associateTag) && settings.siteRegistered;
---
<Layout title="Privacy policy" description="How MyJourney and the serversiderestu Pinterest MCP integration handle website requests, credentials, account information, and privacy requests.">
  <div class="container policy-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1>A small site.<br/>A clear account of data.</h1>
      <p>This notice covers MyJourney and serversiderestu, a private Pinterest MCP integration operated by restupambudi.</p>
      <p>Effective <time datetime="2026-10-15">October 15, 2026</time>.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="correction-box">
        <p>For the app’s data practices, read <a class="text-link" href="#serversiderestu">serversiderestu and Pinterest</a>. For privacy questions about the website or app, email <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${settings.contactEmail}`}>{settings.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <h2 id="serversiderestu">serversiderestu and Pinterest</h2>
      <p>serversiderestu uses a locally running MCP connector to connect Codex to the official Pinterest API for the Pinterest Business account owned and managed by restupambudi. Its intended use is limited to the operator’s own account. It is not offered as a service for managing other people’s accounts.</p>
      <p><strong>Information and purpose.</strong> Depending on the task and granted permissions, the integration processes account information, board names and identifiers, and Pin identifiers, titles, descriptions, links, and media information. It uses these details to display the operator’s account content and prepare requested changes. The operator selects the content and destination board and authorizes each publishing or modification action. Selected content and media are sent to Pinterest when that action is carried out. The intended use does not include scraping Pinterest, collecting passwords or session cookies, selling Pinterest data, or providing competitor research.</p>
      <p><strong>Codex and OpenAI processing.</strong> Requests and relevant Pinterest API responses are made available to Codex and may be processed by OpenAI to carry out the operator’s instructions. Pinterest information therefore does not remain exclusively on the local computer. The local connector has no model-training or fine-tuning functions. OpenAI’s handling of requests and results, including retention and data controls, depends on the applicable service plan, account settings, and policies.</p>
      <p><strong>Credentials and local storage.</strong> The configured Pinterest access token is retained in the operator’s Windows user environment and supplied to the local MCP process. It is sent to Pinterest to authenticate API requests and remains in that local environment until the operator removes or replaces it. The local connector does not maintain a separate database of fetched account, board, or Pin responses; it requests information through the API as needed. Credentials should not be included in chats, public pages, or source repositories.</p>
      <p><strong>History and retention.</strong> Codex conversation history and tool results may be retained locally or by OpenAI according to the product’s configuration, account settings, and applicable policies. This notice does not promise a fixed retention period for those separate systems. Content published to Pinterest remains there until it is separately removed through an authorized action.</p>
      <p><strong>Stopping access and deleting records.</strong> The operator can stop the integration by removing its MCP configuration, deleting local credentials, and revoking the app or token through Pinterest’s controls. Removing a local credential does not itself revoke a token, delete published Pins, or remove Codex conversation history. Those actions must be handled separately through the relevant service’s controls. For a privacy question or deletion request concerning serversiderestu, use the <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      <h2>Reading and searching</h2>
      <p>The current visitor pages have no analytics service, advertising scripts, newsletter signup, shopping account, or contact form. The website does not ask readers to create an account. The site uses system fonts and serves illustration assets with the website.</p>
      <p>Search checks the site’s own editorial content. A search term appears in the page URL as a query parameter. URLs may remain in your browser history and may be recorded in hosting access logs. Do not put personal or sensitive information into a search.</p>
      <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
      <p>MyJourney runs on an owner-managed Ubuntu VPS using Node.js and EmDash, with Cloudflare proxying website traffic over HTTPS. The VPS hosting service, server software, and Cloudflare may process technical request information to deliver and protect the site, such as IP addresses, requested URLs, browser details, and request times. The records retained and their retention periods depend on the deployed server and provider configurations. We do not state a fixed log-retention period because it has not been verified.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and administrator access</h2>
      <p>The current public pages do not set analytics, advertising, or visitor-account cookies. The EmDash CMS administrator area is enabled for authorized editors and processes authentication and session information to control administrator access. It may use authentication or session cookies. Those administrator functions are separate from reading the public guides, and their storage and retention depend on the deployed CMS configuration.</p>
      <h2>Contact and external websites</h2>
      <p>If you email <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${settings.contactEmail}`}>{settings.contactEmail}</a>, the email provider processes your message and its normal delivery information. Correspondence is used to respond to your question, correction, or privacy request. Storage and retention depend on the mailbox settings and handling of the request; this notice does not promise a fixed deletion period. Share only information necessary for your question.</p>
      <p>Reference links take you to other websites when you choose to open them. Those websites apply their own data practices. {affiliateActive ? 'Amazon paid links are explained in our affiliate disclosure.' : 'There are no active affiliate links or affiliate click-tracking scripts in the current editorial-only configuration.'}</p>
      <h2>Questions and changes</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions about MyJourney or serversiderestu, email <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${settings.contactEmail}`}>{settings.contactEmail}</a> or visit <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact and corrections</a>. We will update this notice when hosting, app connections, or data features change and revise the effective date above.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
